{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0009675","label":"autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2A","definition":"Autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2A (LGMD2A) is a subtype of autosomal recessive limb girdle muscular dystrophy characterized by a variable age of onset of progressive, typically symmetrical and selective weakness and atrophy of proximal shoulder- and pelvic-girdle muscles (gluteus maximus, thigh adductors, and muscles of the posterior compartment of the limbs are most commonly affected) without cardiac or facial involvement. Clinical manifestations include exercise intolerance, a waddling gait, scapular winging and calf pseudo-hypertrophy.","synonyms":["CAPN3 autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy","LGMD2","LGMD2A","Leyden-Moebius muscular dystrophy","autosomal recessive limb-girdle muscular dystrophy caused by mutation in CAPN3","calpainopathy","limb-girdle muscular dystrophy due to calpain deficiency","limb-girdle muscular dystrophy type 2"],"xrefs":["DOID:0110275","GARD:0001057","MEDGEN:358391","MESH:C535895","NCIT:C142079","OMIM:253600","Orphanet:267","SCTID:715341003","UMLS:C1869123"],"parents":[],"parents_labels":{},"children":[],"children_labels":{},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":null,"is_group":false,"n_genes":1,"n_phenotypes":27,"mechanism_classes":[]},"genes":[{"id":"e_f56c5ae5ca98","source":"MONDO:0009675","target":"CAPN3","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:267","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/267","confidence":0.95,"snippet":"Disease-causing germline mutation(s) in (Assessed) — calpain 3"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:267","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"url":"https://hpo.jax.org/browse/disease/ORPHA:267","snippet":"CAPN3 is annotated as disease gene of ORPHA:267 (HPO genes_to_phenotype, Orphanet-derived)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.95,"independent_sources":[